WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.116
Normalization separates facts into different tables
so each fact has a clear

00:00:04.142 --> 00:00:10.014
home Later analytical queries reconnect those tables
through keys

00:00:11.751 --> 00:00:16.424
This slide previews that idea with a provided join
query Joins are

00:00:16.451 --> 00:00:19.714
taught step by step in Module 6 so you are not
expected

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:25.080
to write this query yet Run it and inspect the
connected result

00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:32.200
Notice how patient provider appointment service and
service-line information can be combined

00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:37.206
without having stored all of those facts in one
giant table That

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:41.667
is a major benefit of relational design store facts
in well-structured places

00:00:41.956 --> 00:00:47.089
then reconnect them when a question requires a
broader view For now

00:00:47.352 --> 00:00:50.786
focus on recognizing how keys make that reconnection
possible
